  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 19 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s19"><span class="num">19</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Handelsbestand</div><div class="glossary-def">Trading book — a bank's own portfolio of financial instruments and precious metals held for trading purposes.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Fristengliederung</div><div class="glossary-def">Maturity banding — the structured remaining-term breakdown of receivables and liabilities, disclosed exclusively in the Anhang.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Fonds für allgemeine Bankrisiken</div><div class="glossary-def">Fund for general banking risks — a mandatory special reserve, allocated at least 10% of net trading income each year.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">RechKredV</div><div class="glossary-def">Kreditinstituts-Rechnungslegungsverordnung — the separate regulation governing the detailed Formblatt structure this poster does not reproduce in full.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Wirtschaftsprüfer</div><div class="glossary-def">Chartered accountant — the qualification required of at least half a Prüfungsverband's own board for §340k(2)'s cooperative-bank audit rule to apply.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Key</div>
